  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Wired Page",
    "overview": "The page is a small node graph, the way a ComfyUI workflow reads: an About node wires out into two lanes, Film & VFX (Reels, Credits) and AI tools & teaching (Apps, Arctic Latent), and both lanes wire into a Contact node. It stays in the modern minimal developer register: one type size, neutral greys, hairline frames, rows inside every node, on a ground with a faint dot grid. Wires, sockets and title-bar dots carry the only colour: a quiet blue for Film & VFX and a quiet pink for AI tools & teaching. Side by side from 960px, one wired column below. Wires run straight, with right-angle bends and a dot on each bend.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A node graph: About → two lanes → Contact. Side by side from 960px; one wired column below.",
      "One type size (15px), stepped by weight (400/500/600) and colour; 14px only for meta and small print.",
      "Neutral palette, light and dark by `prefers-color-scheme`; colour only on wires, sockets and title-bar dots, one hue per lane.",
      "Rows with 1px hairlines as the universal list form, inside nodes.",
      "Flat: no shadows, no gradients. Nodes are the one framed container, never nested."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
